```

The comment even explicitly describes the bug!

To fix this, I need to implement a bounce. A simple way is to determine which side of the brick was hit.

If the ball is moving UP (vy < 0) and hits the bottom of the brick, it should bounce DOWN (vy > 0).
If the ball is moving DOWN (vy > 0) and hits the top of the brick, it should bounce UP (vy < 0).
If the ball is moving LEFT (vx < 0) and hits the right side, it should bounce RIGHT (vx > 0).
If the ball is moving RIGHT (vx > 0) and hits the left side, it should bounce LEFT (vx < 0).

Wait, the `collides` function only says *if* they overlap. To know *which* side was hit, we can compare the centers or the distance to the edges.

Another approach is to check which axis has the smaller penetration depth.

Let's refine the collision logic.

```javascript
export function collides(ball, brick) {
  return (
    ball.x + ball.r > brick.x &&
    ball.x - ball.r < brick.x + brick.w &&
    ball.y + ball.r > brick.y &&
    ball.y - ball.r < brick.y + brick.h
  );
}
```

